WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.925
Here's Microsoft's starting point.

2
00:00:01.925 --> 00:00:06.941
Learn's Key Vault Private Link page creates
a vault on role-based access with purge

3
00:00:06.941 --> 00:00:11.957
protection, closes its firewall, creates
the vault's privatelink zone and its link,

4
00:00:11.957 --> 00:00:15.350
and the private endpoint,
then validates with nslookup.

5
00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:19.062
It also says name resolution is
where private endpoints fail.

6
00:00:19.062 --> 00:00:22.714
A private DNS zone group
registers the endpoint's record,

7
00:00:22.714 --> 00:00:24.812
and removes it with the endpoint.

8
00:00:24.812 --> 00:00:28.421
The Cloud Adoption Framework
keeps privatelink zones central

9
00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:32.099
in the connectivity subscription
and adds zone groups by policy.

10
00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:35.450
The zone group API
returns each group's zone.

11
00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:40.477
And Learn's Key Vault recommendations:
role-based access, not access policies;

12
00:00:40.477 --> 00:00:46.030
purge protection; private endpoints with
public access disabled; and audit logging.
